  "Heartgate Basin": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — sacred fox-spirit garden-forest. The Demi-Plane's developed heart surrounds its sole intentional threshold in terraces of pale stone, lantern trees, clear rills, flowering orchard, violet moss, and warm-gold foxfire. The Gateway Clearing remains open at the center, but it is framed by a living garden rather than featureless ground. Four ecological gradients meet here: sanctuary woodland and Westreach meadow from the west, Threshold reeds from the north, Dawn Barrow water from the east, and deep prairie roots from the south. The Hearth Springs, Mana Heart, Verdant Plot, Gateway Clearing, and Gate sit within this deliberately composed heartscape.\n\nLiving Ecology: The Basin distributes what the rest of the realm gathers. The Mana Heart supplies measured magical pressure; orchard roots and pale mycelium soften it; spring channels carry it outward; and garden animals disperse seed along the same routes. Nine broad root-streams curve through the soil like fox tails without forming a new mechanic or replacing the established development categories. Lantern koi filter the rills, brush-tail gardeners bury fallen fruit, spirit flowers open to company and close to conflict, and dust-sized mana elementals feed the soil before dissolving at dusk.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 1–12): brush-tail garden foxes, lantern koi, petal quail, jewel beetles, orchard moths, tame spirit fauna, garden spirits already native to the basin, and harmless mana elementals that pool in sunlight like motes of warm glass.\n\nResources: mana fruit, spirit flowers, cultivated herbs, lantern-tree sap, clean springwater, fallen petal-silk, and garden stone produced through established development rather than limitless conjuration.\n\nKnown Locations: The Gateway Clearing with Gateway Chamber and Demi-Plane Gate; Chamberlain's Quarters; Hearth Springs; Mana Heart; and Verdant Plot. Minor garden changes remain personal discoveries rather than new marked facilities.",
    "factions": [],
