  "The Still Frontier": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — cold highland spirit-forest. Pale conifers climb blue-white ridges beneath a sky washed with pearl and winter violet. Their needles hold frost-formed foxfire like tiny sleeping stars; snow falls in slow spirals, and silver breath-mist reveals every moving body before the body itself appears. Southward, the frostpines soften into the cedar, pine, and luminous moss of the Veiled Fox Sanctuary; eastward, their roots break through the white stone of the Pale Reaches. At the outer rim, color, texture, and sound fade together until there is no further world.\n\nLiving Ecology: This is the Demi-Plane's cold reservoir. Frostwood roots draw surplus mana from the ridge, freeze it into clear nodules, and release it during brief violet thaws. Melt-thread runs east into the Pale Reaches and south beneath the sanctuary, while cone-scales carried by frost-tail foxes seed new trees exactly where the boundary gains ground. Tiny icewing moths pollinate winter herbs; glass-antler grazers open paths through deep snow; pale root-mites and blue fungus reduce every fallen branch without rot. The forest is severe, self-renewing, and visibly connected to the warmer woodland below it.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 20–30): frost-tail foxes that leave momentary constellations in their tracks; glass-antler elk browsing frozen lichen; spiral owls riding snow that rises as often as it falls; pale ridge wolves hunting by breath-mist; and non-sapient snow-wraiths that curl into drifts when startled. Healthy predators keep the grazers moving, and nothing here exists merely as an encounter.\n\nResources: naturally fallen frostwood, permanent ice crystal, winter herbs, star-lichen, and frozen foxfire gathered from branches only after it sheds itself.\n\nKnown Locations: Frontier Fade, where willed ground becomes unwilled, and Frostpine Ridge, the forest's high spine. Root-caves, violet thaw pools, frozen nursery groves, and unmoving weather pockets remain discoveries rather than permanent markers.",
    "factions": [],
    "hiddenInfo": "The frontier advances when the Demi-Plane carries an ecological surplus and retreats when the whole realm is strained. The Chamberlain reads its position as a health indicator, but the trees reveal trouble sooner: their foxfire moves from the branch tips toward the trunks before the boundary recedes. Beneath Frostpine Ridge, interlocked roots preserve seeds, spores, insects, and sleeping spirit-fauna for every northern biome. The region is not an empty edge awaiting construction; it is the realm's winter memory and recovery vault.",
