  "The Pale Reaches": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — misty white-stone highland badland. White terraces, shallow gullies, and low stone benches lie under a silver sky. Mist gathers ankle-deep in the valleys and glows from within; silver lichen freckles the rock in patterns like unfamiliar constellations. The terrain receives frostwater from the Still Frontier, loosens into luminous meadow soil to the south, and gathers into wet river-grass toward the North Field. Colors remain restrained—milk-white, lavender-grey, and points of cold blue—yet the ground constantly produces fleeting arches, groves, and distant hills that vanish when approached.\n\nLiving Ecology: Raw dimensional mist acts here as soil, weather, and nursery. Star-lichen fixes loose potential into stone; pale cup-fungi drink it back out; fogmice carry lichen spores between benches; and stoneback browsers scrape mineral crusts loose for smaller creatures. Condensed mist drains east into the Shining Channels and south as dawn dew, feeding both North Field reeds and First Meadow flowers. Temporary vegetation appears after a heavy fogfall, lives a complete miniature season in hours, then dissolves into silver pollen that enriches permanent life beyond the Reaches.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 18–30): fogmice with light visible through their ears; stoneback browsers whose hides mimic the benches; pearl-foot hares that vanish against mist; low-floating veil skates feeding on silver spores; and unfinished, non-sapient potential-beasts that briefly borrow a familiar animal shape before returning to fog.\n\nResources: silver lichen, clean white stone, condensed dimensional mist, pale crystal, and short-lived ghost blossoms harvested before they return to vapor.\n\nKnown Locations: Ghost Valleys and Silver-Lichen Flats. Fleeting bridges, gardens, caves, and entire miniature landscapes remain intentionally unmarked because the land completes and erases them as part of its natural cycle.",
    "factions": [],
