  "The Veiled Edge": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — luminous boundary-scrub. Low silver spirit-grass and glass-leaf shrubs spread beneath an aurora that travels through the ground instead of the sky. The scrub thins into a cool, translucent curtain at the northeastern limit, rippling like a lake held upright. Westward, the land gathers into the Fold's pleats; southward, dew thickens, the light darkens to violet, and the first pools of the Mirror Mere appear. Each blade carries a line of colored light from root to tip, so passing animals send waves of emerald, rose, and foxfire-blue through the plain.\n\nLiving Ecology: Boundary light is the primary energy source. Silver grass drinks it through its roots, veil moths pollinate the glass-leaf scrub, aurora hares crop old blades, and translucent veil skates glide inches above the ground feeding on released light-seed. Their waste becomes opaline grit that washes toward Mirror Mere and gives its water a memory-bright sheen. Nothing crosses the curtain as part of the food web; the ecosystem feeds on harmless light and residue shed inward by the boundary itself.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 22–30): veil moths with window-clear wings; aurora hares; low-gliding veil skates; prism-backed beetles; quiet boundary walkers shaped like long-legged deer but without faces; and shoals of foxfire minnows swimming through dense ground-light after dusk.\n\nResources: veilglass, aurora crystal, silver spirit-grass, glass-leaf resin, and boundary essence gathered only after the curtain sheds a stable droplet on its own.\n\nKnown Locations: The Shimmering Curtain and Veilwatch Point. Light hollows, moth nurseries, and temporary views through layered color remain discoveries along the living edge.",
    "hiddenInfo": "Focused intent thins the curtain enough to reveal distant leylines and pocket dimensions, but the local ecology also protects it. When pressure gathers from outside, every grass blade goes dark at once, moths settle, and boundary walkers align facing the same point. Their behavior gives warning before wards register a breach. Harvesting live veilgrass at that moment would break the warning chain; fallen blades retain the same crafting value and regrow naturally.",
