  "The First Meadow": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — luminous wildflower meadow. Rolling silver-green grass carries cobalt foxfire blooms, moonlace flowers, amber bellcups, and pale petals that turn toward warmth instead of sunlight. Pollen rises in slow spirals at dawn and settles like warm snow at dusk. The Sanctuary's trees thin into flowered shade along the west; white-stone dust from the Pale Reaches enriches the north; eastward the grasses lengthen into the Threshold March; southward scattered saplings announce the Westreach. The Beginning's Torii stands at the northwest crossing, clearly visible without making the private sanctuary accessible.\n\nLiving Ecology: This is the realm's principal pollination meadow and the clearest proof that it grows without constant direction. Violetwing moths emerge from the Sanctuary, spirit butterflies arrive on Reaches mist, and duskbees build translucent comb beneath grass hummocks. Meadow foxes distribute buried mana-fruit seeds; ribbon hares trim fast-growing shoots; petal mice gather spent pollen into warm nests where new fungi begin. The Meadow exchanges seed with every adjacent region and prevents any single magical plant from becoming a monoculture.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 1–10): meadow foxes, ribbon hares, petal mice, violetwing moths, spirit butterflies, duskbees, flower-backed tortoises, and gentle grass grazers whose coats take on the colors of the blooms they last ate.\n\nResources: foxfire blooms, moonlace blooms, spirit pollen, silver-green grass, dusk honey, meadow herbs, and naturally shed butterfly glass.\n\nKnown Locations: Beginning's Torii, Fox Statues, and Sanctuary Approach. Seasonal flower rings, pollinator nests, warm-snow pollenfalls, and tiny natural cairns stay unmarked.",
    "factions": [],
    "hiddenInfo": "The Meadow is a maturity gauge, but not merely because grass survives. Its number of simultaneous bloom colors records how many regions are exchanging nutrients successfully. When one biome is strained, its corresponding color disappears from the Meadow within days. The fox statues at the Torii sit above the thickest mycelial junction and quietly keep sanctuary foxfire from overwhelming gentler meadow species.",
