  "The Threshold March": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — open approach-grassland. A broad corridor of low reeds, resilient grass, and pale paths joins Heartgate Basin to the North Field. Reed-seeds drift like slow lanterns, while thin lines of violet foxfire pulse under the turf in time with the Mana Heart. Meadow color enters from the west; mossy stone shoulders rise to the east; water and wind widen northward. The land remains open enough to travel and watch the sky, but it is never bare: every path-edge carries low star-flower, curlfern, or glass-tipped seedgrass.\n\nLiving Ecology: The March is a living artery rather than a road. Its roots sheath the main mana channels, preventing erosion and feeding on harmless leakage. Path beetles loosen compressed soil, wind hares move reed-seed north and south, and lantern cranes rest here during migrations between North Field and Mirror Mere. The trails shift by inches as the internal flow changes, steering feet away from new burrows, wet ground, and flowering beds without obstructing passage.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 3–12): wind hares, lantern cranes, reed voles, path beetles, grass-skimming foxlets, flocking wind-sprites, and brief non-sapient mana constructs shaped like pale animals that complete one circuit before dissolving into the paths.\n\nResources: luminous reed-seed, pathway herbs, mana-rich soil from naturally turned patches, shed crane plumes, and glass-tipped grass harvested after seeding.\n\nKnown Locations: Northern Approach and Mana-Flow Paths. Animal crossings, temporary pools, migrating flocks, and new path branches appear dynamically and remain discoveries rather than settlements or quest dispensers.",
    "factions": [],
    "hiddenInfo": "The paths map the Demi-Plane's circulation more accurately than any instrument. A clear parallel flow means the realm is healthy; braiding indicates rapid growth; knots show strain. Walking them does not create mana, but contact with their leakage restores a small amount of ambient magical equilibrium. The March also functions as a quarantine corridor: when a foreign substance enters through Heartgate, the nearest path bends around it until the ecosystem has tested it.",
