  "The Stone Rise": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — rocky moss-highland. Grey ridges lift through terraces of emerald, cobalt, and silver lichen. Mineral springs thread down bare stone in shining lines, and crystal seams glow beneath translucent moss. The highland receives Fold scrub along its northern shelves, descends west into the Threshold grass, pours water east into the Mirror Mere, and warms south into the redstone banks of Dawn Barrow. From the High Outlook, the Demi-Plane reads as one continuous tapestry rather than separate tiles.\n\nLiving Ecology: Stone, water, and living mineral form one slow cycle. Lichen dissolves trace elements from the ridge; spring-snails concentrate them into discarded pearl shells; cliff goats crop the lichen and carry spores between terraces; stone-boring beetles open channels for water; and moss seals fractures before they widen. Mineral runoff feeds the Mere and Dawn Stream, while migrating drakes bring prairie seed north on their scales. Mining that follows shed stone and exposed seams renews naturally; careless excavation would interrupt the realm's hydrology and structural bedrock.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 8–20): moss-horn goats, cliff drakes, spring-snails with translucent shells, stone-boring beetles, pebble foxes, crystal-wing swifts, and non-sapient mineral elementals that surface briefly where springwater meets a rich seam.\n\nResources: iron-rich stone, spirit mineral, spring pearl, lichen, mineral water, naturally exposed ore, and crystal moss trimmed without stripping the bedrock.\n\nKnown Locations: Mineral Springs, High Outlook, and Foundation Ridge. Caves, narrow passes, crystal chambers, and small spring basins remain open to discovery.",
    "factions": [],
    "hiddenInfo": "Foundation Ridge is structural bedrock for the entire plane, and the spring network is its pressure release. The Mana Heart's guardian patrols it because a collapsed channel would alter water flow from Mirror Mere to Dawn Barrow and stress the Last Edge anchor. Moss color provides warning: emerald marks healthy flow, cobalt marks high mana pressure, and silver marks stone under strain. This makes the highland readable without turning every change into a construction problem.",
