  "The Hollow Vale": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — sheltered terraced vale. Wide stone terraces descend through still warm air, their walls furred with foxfire moss and their banks planted by wind with medicinal root, bellflower, and velvet grass. The northern slopes meet Westreach pasture; eastern terraces open onto the Deep Expanse; southern steps fade into Grey Boundary moor; western seepage feeds the Low Reaches. Foxfire settles along each terrace rim after sunset like lanterns placed by the land itself.\n\nLiving Ecology: The terraces are both habitat and water-control. Spirit clay holds moisture, burrowing moon-rabbits aerate the banks, terrace wrens distribute root seed, and mossback pangolins keep ant and beetle populations balanced. Small springs move down one step at a time, depositing mineral-rich silt before entering the marsh. Empty future building plots remain covered in low, recoverable life until actual development begins; the ecosystem does not pretend a population is already present.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 4–14): moon-rabbits, terrace wrens, mossback pangolins, velvet field mice, gentle earth-spirit creatures, and small dusk foxes that sleep in sun-warmed clay niches.\n\nResources: spirit clay, medicinal roots, terrace herbs, foxfire moss, spring silt, and naturally shed mossback scales used as durable charm blanks.\n\nKnown Locations: Residential Terraces and Sheltered Vale. Springs, small caves, viewpoints, and animal dens remain unmarked and must be discovered without inventing residents.",
    "factions": [],
    "hiddenInfo": "The terraces echo proportions from the Hidden Estate because Tsukiko's sense of shelter shaped the realm's foundational memory. They are not copies and contain no hidden houses or people. Each terrace has a different soil temperament—rest, cultivation, gathering, or foundation—which appears through flower color and drainage. The Chamberlain's development plans work best when they read those signals instead of assigning every step the same function.",
