  "The Open Horizon": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — endless flat savanna. Level gold-green grass runs beneath an enormous sky, with a warm ember line at every horizon. Deep Expanse tallgrass lowers into the north, Grey Boundary moisture enriches the west, Fade mist feathers the east, and the far south remains open light and land. Skywatch Rise is the only deliberate interruption. At night, stars appear both above and within dew on the grass, making travelers feel suspended between two skies.\n\nLiving Ecology: The Horizon is the southern migration and seed-distribution plain. Wind hares, horizon deer, low-floating sky rays, and wandering mana birds follow invisible currents between the Expanse, Grey Boundary, and Fade. Grass roots spread the filtered western water widely; sun-dried herbs store heat from Southroll winds; windseed travels north during one half of the daily cycle and south during the other. Predators hunt in full view, so speed, camouflage, and herd behavior matter more than surprise.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 10–20): wind hares, horizon deer, sky rays drifting at eye height, mana birds, ember-maned coursers, glasswing locusts, and lean open-ground foxes that use mirage rather than cover.\n\nResources: horizon grass, windseed, sun-dried herbs, naturally surfaced ambient mana crystal, glasswing husks, and dew gathered before the lower stars fade.\n\nKnown Locations: Skywatch Rise and Open Horizon Plain. Migratory resting circles, lone crystal blooms, temporary camps made only by permitted visitors, and wind-carved patterns remain unmarked.",
