  "The Last Edge": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — still stony plain. Smooth grey stone, sparse white lichen, motionless air, and directionless light occupy the far southeastern corner. Nothing casts a shadow. Rift March clefts flatten along the north, Fade mist thins at the west, and every further direction becomes the certainty of no more world. The Dimensional Anchor Point interrupts the plain with exact geometry; elsewhere, color appears only in minute violet seams that brighten once each cycle like a sleeping pulse.\n\nLiving Ecology: Life is deliberately sparse but not absent. Anchor lichens metabolize imperceptible dimensional drift; fixed-point beetles crawl the same closed routes for years; grey needle-foxes drink condensation from stone pores; and rare sentinel moths emerge only when the anchor's pulse changes. They require almost nothing and produce almost nothing, forming a minimal maintenance ecology suited to the realm's fixed coordinate.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 25–30): fixed-point beetles, grey needle-foxes, sentinel moths, rare anchor sentinels formed by existing defenses, and silent dimensional creatures that cross the plain without nesting. Any ordinary animal found here is out of range and therefore significant.\n\nResources: nullstone, grey crystal, fixed-point fragments shed naturally from stressed seams, anchor lichen, and sentinel-moth dust gathered only after emergence.\n\nKnown Locations: The Last Edge and Dimensional Anchor Point. Other discoveries stay rare: exact geometric growths, a single changed stone, or an object whose presence has a concrete path rather than invented ancient habitation.",
    "factions": [],
    "hiddenInfo": "The Last Edge is the coordinate from which the Demi-Plane's geometry is extrapolated. Foundation Ridge carries its force northward and the Grey Boundary fixes orientation westward. Its tiny ecology is an early-warning instrument: beetles alter their closed paths before drift, lichen darkens before a fracture, and sentinel moths emerge before the Mana Heart can register misalignment. Destabilization would set the realm drifting from its mortal connection, so harvesting is limited to material the anchor naturally sheds.",
