  "Veiled Fox Sanctuary": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — sanctuary spirit-forest. Mist-laced woodland surrounds a luminous bamboo spring, a vast shinboku, vermilion torii processions, and the hidden grounds of Tsukiko's estate. Pale cedar, pine, maple, sakaki, bamboo, and white-barked foxwood rise in deliberate layers, yet no row feels planted. Violet, cobalt, and warm-gold foxfire travels from mushroom to moss to lantern without burning anything. Sunbeams arrive at impossible angles; water tastes faintly of rain on cedar; shadows occasionally resemble a fox's tail before becoming ordinary shade. The forest cools into frostpine at the north, opens into the First Meadow to the east, and sends moonlit rootwater beneath the Quiet Shore and Westreach to the south.\n\nLiving Ecology: Tsukiko designed the sanctuary as the Demi-Plane's living filter and seed-vault. The shinboku's root crown receives raw power, pale fungi separate it into gentler currents, foxglow caps and lantern trees store excess, and springwater carries balanced mana outward. Moon-antler deer prune saplings, velvet foxes bury luminous fruit, bell-throat thrushes distribute sacred berries, and violetwing moths pollinate blooms that open only in foxfire. Fallen wood is consumed by blue lace-fungus and becomes warm, fertile loam rather than ordinary rot. Nothing is decorative: even the moss-paths protect mycelial channels by guiding feet around them.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 12–25): velvet foxes with harmless tail-lights; moon-antler deer; bell-throat thrushes; violetwing moths; lantern koi in the spring; inkpaw martens; sacred cranes; and small foxfire wisps that behave like curious animals. Beyond the already established estate attendants and shrine guardians, the sanctuary holds no village or wild sapient population; its free-ranging life consists of animals and spirit-creatures.\n\nResources: foxglow caps, foxfire blooms, lantern-tree sap, sacred bamboo, shrine herbs, naturally fallen spirit wood, shinboku leaf-silver, and springwater taken only from the overflow channels.\n\nKnown Locations: The Hidden Estate of the Mother Fox, Shinboku, Bamboo Spring, and Torii Procession. Private garden paths, old shrine niches, animal nurseries, and root-lit groves reveal themselves only through exploration and Tsukiko's permission.",
    "factions": [],
    "hiddenInfo": "The sanctuary admits only those Tsukiko has permitted; no path, spell, status, or intuition overrides her will. Its lanterns read intent, while the forest redirects rather than merely obstructs: roots alter footing, fragrance erases a false trail, and moths extinguish their wings until an intruder circles back out. The shinboku stores a reserve of Tsukiko's aether beneath the estate, but the wider root-and-fungus network distributes ordinary life-supporting mana throughout the western regions. Damaging the sanctuary would disrupt water purity, pollination, and soil renewal far beyond its borders.",
